{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only two data points: RNA-only (pca_n2000, singleprofile) at 0.485 acc and multimodal (pca_n2000 + resnet50, concat, singleprofile) at 0.527 acc. The ~4% gain from adding the image is meaningful, but we cannot yet determine whether this gain reflects genuine complementary information from fusion or simply that the image features are a stronger predictor on their own. Testing config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) establishes the image-only baseline, directly isolating the image modality's independent contribution. This is the single most informative missing piece: if image-only is near 0.52, the multimodal gain is modest and fusion strategy matters less; if image-only is well below 0.48, the multimodal model is extracting real complementary signal and fusion/aggregation choices become high-value next questions. Under a tight budget with sparse evidence, reducing uncertainty about this fundamental modality-contribution question is more valuable than prematurely optimizing fusion type or profile setting, which would be harder to interpret without the image baseline."
}

